SALMONpy third-party notices

The bundled SALMON-derived kernels use the repository's Apache-2.0 license.
Platform wheels can include OpenBLAS and GCC/Fortran runtimes; their notices are
preserved in packaging/ld/licenses/ and installed as salmonpy/licenses/:

- OpenBLAS-LICENSE.txt
- GCC-RUNTIME-EXCEPTION.txt
- GPL-3.0.txt
- LGPL-2.1.txt
- NOTICE.txt

macOS kernel wheels link the operating system Accelerate framework.
Python dependencies (NumPy and optional ASE/f90nml/Matplotlib) retain their own
installed licenses; they are dependencies, not copied Python source here.

The optional external full SALMON runtime has its own LICENSE.THIRD-PARTY and
ACKNOWLEDGEMENTS, obtained from the pinned upstream source. Its FFTE, bundled
linear algebra, Libxc and other application-specific notices are not replaced
by this package notice. No FFTE, full LAPACK or full SALMON application sources
are bundled in SALMONpy's native/ directory.
